5,1,1,talk,Toshio,,We should start by asking what actually worked. I want to look into the post-occupancy review ratings and the decade of delivery schedules.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Toshio. I want to examine the timetable records on rooms out of service and the booking data for specialist and general rooms.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,I’ve watched the same few people absorb every new burden for years. I’ll check the staffing posts since the hiring freeze and the bench technicians' weekly manual routines.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,I need to see the weather days in the site diaries and the survey findings in the older blocks.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,I’ll review the tender records over three budget cycles and the renewal reserve for equipment bought earlier.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Benjamin"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Benjamin: I’ll review the tender records over three budget cycles and the renewal reserve for equipment bought earlier.""}]}"
10,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, your focus on the physical constraints is prudent. I am curious if the schedule slips you anticipate correlate with the specific project rationales I am investigating.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I suspect the schedule slips you mention are directly tied to the off-site replacement costs I am tracking.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, your focus on the paper figures is wise. I am concerned that the physical labor costs are being ignored in those projections.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the physical labor you mention is exactly what the weather and survey delays will compound. I need to see how those constraints squeeze the calendar.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, the labor you cite is real, but the capital figures I am tracking have drifted further from market reality. We must reconcile the two before deciding.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, your point about off-site costs is valid. I am looking for evidence that projects driven by inspection findings actually deliver on time, unlike those based on comfort.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, that distinction is crucial. If comfort-driven projects slip, the timetable absorbs the delay, and the rooms sit empty. I need to see if that pattern holds.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,George,,"@Toshio, I appreciate the focus on delivery. However, if the work slips, the same exhausted staff absorb the backlog. I need to know if the routine load is already critical.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the backlog you describe is exactly what the weather and survey delays will trigger. I need to see how those constraints squeeze the calendar.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, the calendar squeeze is real, but the price tag is the silent killer. I need to know if the approved figures even survive the first tender round.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the price drift is a serious concern. I will see if the delivery data confirms that financial uncertainty correlates with the schedule failures I am tracking.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, the financial drift is critical, but I need to know if the empty rooms are a symptom of that cost or a failure of planning.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, the cost drift is real, but the human cost is immediate. I need to know if the unfilled posts mean the routine upkeep is already failing before the new work even starts.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Benjamin, the cost drift is real, but the calendar is the immediate bottleneck. I need to see if the physical delays force us to compress the work into the few weeks left.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, the calendar is the symptom; the budget is the disease. If the tender prices exceed the approved figures, the work stops regardless of the weather.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
