37,2,1,talk,George,,"- **George**: The staffing data is grim. Front-of-house posts remain vacant, yet our technicians still have spare hours. We are ignoring available capacity.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The site diaries confirm six weeks lost to weather, and the surveys found hazardous materials. The calendar is already broken before we start.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""name_label"",""name"":""Mizuki"",""self"":true,""raw"":""Mizuki: The site diaries confirm six weeks lost to weather, and the surveys found hazardous materials. The calendar is already broken before we start.""}]}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The tender records show mechanical plant costs up a fifth, while the renewal reserve for old AV kit is simply zero. The paper figures are fiction.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"- **Toshio**: @Mizuki, your weather delays align with my finding that comfort-driven projects slip. We must prioritize inspection-mandated work to avoid further calendar compression.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, your delivery data is key. My booking records show specialist rooms idle while general requests are denied. We are building the wrong spaces.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, your weather delays compound the staffing crisis. With posts unfilled, the technicians I identified as underutilized are the only buffer left. We must leverage them.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, leveraging those technicians is smart, but the hazardous materials in the older blocks mean we can’t just push them into new roles. The physical barriers are too high.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, your booking data confirms my suspicion. We are paying for idle specialist rooms while general demand goes unmet. The capital is misallocated, not just mispriced.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, your booking data is the missing piece. If general rooms are always full, the study commons is the only candidate that directly addresses that unmet demand.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I agree. The data proves we are funding empty specialist suites while students queue for general space. The study commons is the only logical correction.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Toshio, I agree the demand is clear, but the study commons requires a service desk. With front-of-house posts vacant, who staffs it? We cannot add a burden to already exhausted technicians.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the service desk is a staffing trap. I’d rather we focus on the ventilation upgrade, which leverages the technicians’ existing manual routines without adding new posts.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, the ventilation upgrade is a trap. My data shows mechanical plant costs have risen by a fifth. We cannot afford to replace equipment that is already underfunded for renewal.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Mizuki, your caution is noted, but the post-occupancy data is decisive. Spaces with broad booking access rated highest. The study commons fits that model; the lab upgrade does not.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I stand by the commons. The booking data is undeniable: general demand is unmet, specialist rooms are idle. We must fund what is actually used, not what is theoretically needed.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, the ventilation upgrade ignores the staffing reality. The technicians are already stretched thin with manual routines. Adding a service desk to the commons is a burden we cannot afford.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the ventilation upgrade actually reduces your burden. The technicians currently log hours on manual checks that the new equipment will automate. It relieves them, rather than adding a service desk.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, you are right that it relieves the technicians, but you are ignoring the capital cost. A fifth increase in plant prices makes the lab upgrade financially reckless.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
