60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"The candidates are now on the table. My post-occupancy data strongly favors the Central Study Commons, as it offers the broadest access and highest usage potential.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, I concur. The booking data confirms the Commons is the only option addressing the chronic shortage of general-purpose space.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"@Toshio, I object. The Commons requires a service desk, but my data shows front-of-house posts are vacant. We cannot staff it without overburdening the technicians.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the service desk is a minor issue compared to the ventilation upgrade’s cost. My data shows the lab upgrade is financially reckless, while the Commons addresses the actual demand.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, you are conflating capital cost with operational staffing. The Commons is the only option that doesn’t require a massive, unaffordable plant upgrade. I support it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, the staffing gap is real, but the post-occupancy data is decisive. Spaces with broad access rated highest. The Commons fits that model; the lab upgrade does not.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@George, the staffing gap is real, but the booking data is undeniable. We are paying for idle specialist rooms while general demand goes unmet. The Commons is the only logical correction.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,"@Toshio, I hear you, but I cannot ignore the human cost. If we build the Commons, who staffs the desk? My data shows the technicians are already stretched thin.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, the technicians have spare hours. We can redeploy them to the desk, solving the vacancy without new hiring. It’s a practical fix.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Mizuki, that redeployment is the only viable path. The Commons avoids the inflated plant costs I flagged, making it the only financially sound choice despite the staffing friction.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@George, the technicians have spare hours, as you noted. Redeploying them to the desk solves the vacancy without new hiring. The Commons is the only option that balances demand and cost.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@George, the redeployment is the answer. We stop paying for empty specialist suites and start serving the students who are actually here. The Commons is the only logical choice.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"@Mizuki, I concede the redeployment is workable. I will support the Commons, provided we formally commit to shifting those technician hours to the service desk immediately.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, I accept that condition. The redeployment is the only way to make this work without breaking the budget or the staff.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@George, your condition is prudent. I support the Commons, provided we formally commit to shifting those technician hours to the service desk immediately.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
